\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
Development economics context.
\series default
 The fictional app places harvest insurance and digital contracting in a rural setting. Townsend (1994) studies consumption insurance in Indian villages, Udry (1994) studies state contingent rural loan repayments in Nigeria, and Jack and Suri (2014) study mobile money and risk sharing in Kenya. These studies motivate the setting; the app, harvest quantities, and fully enforceable market are assumptions of the exercise. 
