\begin_layout Standard
The box redistributes 3 units in dry weather and 6 in rainy weather. Contracts cannot change those totals. Both households cannot have constant consumption across states while consuming the full harvest: their combined constant consumption would have to equal both 3 and 6. At equilibrium A consumes 
\begin_inset Formula $5/9$
\end_inset

 and B consumes 
\begin_inset Formula $4/9$
\end_inset

 of the total harvest in either state. They share aggregate risk rather than eliminate it. Zero portfolio value is a price weighted condition, distinct from zero expected grain transfers.
\end_layout

