\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
Walrasian equilibrium.
\series default
 Choose 
\begin_inset Formula $p=(1,1)$
\end_inset

. Both endowments have wealth 4, so each budget is 
\begin_inset Formula $x_i+y_i\le4$
\end_inset

. For every affordable bundle, 
\begin_inset Formula \[
 \sqrt{x_i y_i}\le\frac{x_i+y_i}{2}\le2.
\]
\end_inset

Equality holds at 
\begin_inset Formula $(2,2)$
\end_inset

, establishing global demand optimality directly. The two demands sum to 
\begin_inset Formula $(4,4)$
\end_inset

 and clear both markets. Thus the terminal allocation and these prices form a Walrasian equilibrium.
\end_layout

