\series bold
Benchmark and net welfare.
\series default
 From part (a), aggregate goods utility is at most 4. At the terminal allocation both consumers obtain 2, so the frictionless benchmark is 
\begin_inset Formula $W^*=4$
\end_inset

. Other diagonal allocations also attain aggregate utility 4; the assigned trading procedure selects equal division. Using the supplied utility and time units, 
\begin_inset Formula \[
 W^{\mathrm m}=\sum_i(U_i-C_i^{\mathrm m})=4-(C_A^{\mathrm m}+C_B^{\mathrm m}),
 \qquad \mathrm m\in\{\mathrm H,\mathrm B\}.
\]
\end_inset

