\series bold
Decomposition.
\series default
 For either method, 
\begin_inset Formula \[
 L^{\mathrm m}
 =\underbrace{\bigl[4-(U_A+U_B)\bigr]}_{\text{goods allocation loss}}
 +\underbrace{C_A^{\mathrm m}+C_B^{\mathrm m}}_{\text{negotiation cost}}.
\]
\end_inset

Both methods reach the same goods allocation, with 
\begin_inset Formula $U_A+U_B=4$
\end_inset

. Goods allocation loss is therefore zero. The entire remaining loss is owner attention cost, which falls from 0.16 to 0.04 with the bot. This explains the welfare gain at unchanged terminal consumption and supporting goods prices.
